## Core features
- One MCM, one ESP and one DLL. Chaurus, Spider and Dwemer each have their own attack, animation and pregnancy settings
- Choose solo Estrus animations or creature scenes. Preview included animations without triggering Unified pregnancy
- Skeleton scaling or body morphs for CBBE / 3BA and UUNP / BHUNP, with optional SLIF and Ovibody support
- Separate attack cooldown and post-scene calm timers, settings remembered across saves, and pregnancy and hatchery tracking
### Optional Chaurus and Spider companions
Companions is optional and off by default. Enable it in the Companions tab to raise Chaurus and Spider hatchlings. Eligible offspring from active followers can join your roster too.

Raise and name your companions. By default they reach Juvenile at 1 day, Adolescent at 4 days and Adult at 6 in-game days. Feeding them speeds up growth
Carry babies on your back to protect them. Up to five are visible at once, and each carried baby adds 5 carry weight. Babies do not use summon slots
Summon grown companions from the ground with a snap, then use the command wheel to direct them. Five active summons by default; configurable up to 25
Order them to attack, feed, wait, follow or burrow away. Choose Passive or Aggressive behavior. 
Hatchlings can have different patterns and colors, and keep their look as they grow
